// @summary:    a call to a missing procedure inside a procedure that never runs, which only validation can catch
// @error-kind: validation
// @error:      Procedure `missing' is not defined
//
// A call to a procedure that is never defined.  The interpreter would only
// notice if the caller ran, and here it never does -- but the C++ back-end has
// to resolve every name, so validation rejects it up front.

procedure helper(int x)
    call missing(x)

procedure main()
    int a
    a += 1
